    "checks": [
      "An accessory apartment needs a special exception from the Zoning Hearing Board in R-1, R-2 and R-3 (205-22B, 205-25B, 205-28B)",
      "Only with a single-family detached house. One accessory apartment per lot",
      "Inside the house: at most 30% of the house floor area. In an accessory building: at most 650 sq ft",
      "The lot must meet the district minimum lot area for a single-family detached house (R-1 10,000, R-2 6,500, R-3 5,000 sq ft)",
      "The house or accessory building with the apartment must meet the district yards for a single-family detached house",
      "The house must keep one front entrance. Other entrances go on the side or rear. Exterior stairs go on the rear wall where possible",
      "Parking: the house spaces plus one space per bedroom in the apartment (205-120)",
      "Sewer authority certification of capacity is needed. A septic system needs Bucks County Department of Health approval",
      "The code sets no owner-occupancy or family rule for an accessory apartment",
      "No height is set for a building with an apartment. Sheds are capped at 12 ft and garages at 16 ft (205-16G(2)(h))",
      "Separate option: Use A6 Residential Conversion turns an existing building into two or three units. It is also a special exception in R-1 to R-3"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Building and Planning Department, https://www.bristoltwppa.gov/349/Building-Planning-Department. Pending: none found on eCode360 New Laws for Chapter 205. Do not confuse with Bristol Borough."
  },
